  "problem": "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,11{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+12{x}_{1}+16{x}_{2}=20.\n$$\n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)=11{x}_{1}^{2}-24{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $20{y}_{2}^{2}-5{y}_{1}^{2}$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$",
